# source: spec
# spec: docs/protocol/compression-lzc.md#end-of-stream
# provenance: PV-0060, PV-0061, PV-0062, PV-0063, PV-0065, PV-0066, PV-0067, PV-0069, PV-0080, PV-0350, PV-0310, PV-0312, PV-0384, PV-0385, PV-0386, PV-0388, PV-0391, PV-0392, PV-0395, PV-0314
# kind: decompress
# description: Valid data that decodes to 7 bytes under a header that declares 8.
# derivation: Header: length 8, byte 7 0x90. Data exactly as in lzc-code-equals-next-free. After its four codes 4 bits remain, fewer than 9, and no further chunk exists, so the stream ends with 7 bytes output (PV-0395); 7 differs from 8, so decoding fails with length-mismatch (PV-0314, IMPL-LZC-2).
# expect.error: length-mismatch
# expect.algorithm: lzc
# expect.uncompressed_length: 8
# expect.block_mode: 1
hex:
08 00 00 00                                       # uncompressed length, u32 LE
11                                                # algorithm byte
1F 9D                                             # magic
90                                                # byte 7
41 84 04 1C 08                                    # as lzc-code-equals-next-free
